[statement]
Reduced from Alpine v3.24 (`main` and `community`, 2026-11-08), asked for
`akonadi-calendar`, over the records the request can reach and those whose
`install_if` names one of them. Two `install_if` conditions that never
hold, since nothing provides `lang`, lead the walk for the preliminary
choices from `iso-codes-lang` to `lang`, from `lang` to `pimcommon-lang`,
and from its condition to `pimcommon`, whose dependencies reach
`so:libKF6Wallet.so.6` before `dbus:org.freedesktop.Secrets`: `kwallet`,
the one candidate for the first, is chosen for it, and then for the
second, which it answers
(`decision-order/a-name-a-choice-answers-takes-that-package`);
`gnome-keyring` is not installed. Without either condition
(`conditions-that-never-hold-steer-a-choice-without-one`) `gnome-keyring`
is installed for the second. Over the whole index, with more `install_if`
records, apk installs `gnome-keyring` too
(`reduced/akonadi-calendar-takes-gnome-keyring`). The shape of
`a-condition-that-never-holds-reserves-a-provider`.

